\f0\b\fs36 \cf2 \strokec2 1. Inspect Before Implementing\cf2 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf2 \strokec2 Before writing or modifying code, thoroughly inspect the existing VHSart project, its folder structure, rendering pipeline, noise generators, horizontal streak/dropout systems, compositing utilities, preset architecture, and parameter registration.\
Identify which existing engines can already generate:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\ls2\ilvl0\cf2 \strokec2 {\listtext	\'95	}Horizontal luma streaks and fragmented scanline segments.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Dark-field noise and dropout patterns.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Variable horizontal segment lengths.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Spatial density gradients.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Per-frame deterministic variation.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Screen/Add/input blending.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \strokec2 Reuse and extend existing implementations wherever technically appropriate. Do not create duplicate engines or replace functioning systems unnecessarily.\
Do not modify unrelated presets or break existing functionality.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf2 \strokec2 2. Visual Target\cf2 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf2 \strokec2 Reconstruct the reference as a monochrome, dark-field horizontal streak effect.\
The visual identity must include:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\ls3\ilvl0\cf2 \strokec2 {\listtext	\'95	}A predominantly black or very dark background.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Thin and medium-width horizontal white, light-gray, and dim-gray streak segments.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Sparse streaks in the upper third.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Gradually increasing streak density through the middle.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Strong concentration and partial visual clustering toward the bottom edge.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Continuously changing streak positions, lengths, and brightness across frames.\
{\listtext	\'95	}A consistent bottom-heavy density profile throughout the animation.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \strokec2 The result must resemble horizontal luma dropouts and scanline tearing, not ordinary random noise.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf2 \strokec2 3. Core Spatial Distribution\cf2 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf2 \strokec2 Implement a genuine vertical density distribution.\
Use normalized vertical coordinates:\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f2 \cf2 \strokec2 yNorm = y / (height - 1)
\f1 \cf2 \strokec2 \
Calculate a configurable bottom-weighting function:\

\f2 \cf2 \strokec2 bottomWeight = pow(yNorm, gradientExponent)
\f1 \cf2 \strokec2 \
Use this weighting to control the probability of generating horizontal streak segments.\
The upper region must remain substantially darker and less populated than the lower region.\
The density transition must be smooth and configurable, without producing an obvious artificial boundary between regions.\
Do not simulate this effect by simply increasing overall noise intensity.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf2 \strokec2 4. Horizontal Streak Generation\cf2 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf2 \strokec2 Generate horizontal segments procedurally using deterministic hash-based sampling.\
Each segment should have independently controlled properties:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\ls4\ilvl0\cf2 \strokec2 {\listtext	\'95	}Horizontal starting position.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Segment length.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Thickness.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Luma intensity.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Local contrast.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Probability of appearing.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Temporal variation.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \strokec2 Support short, medium, and occasional longer horizontal segments.\
Avoid:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\ls5\ilvl0\cf2 \strokec2 {\listtext	\'95	}Circular or point-shaped noise.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Large continuous horizontal bars dominating the image.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Vertical lines.\
{\listtext	\'95	}RGB channel separation.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Chroma bleeding.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Unrequested geometric distortion.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \strokec2 All generated streaks must remain monochromatic, with equal RGB values.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf2 \strokec2 5. Temporal Behavior\cf2 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf2 \strokec2 The reference shows continuously changing streak distributions between frames while preserving the same overall bottom-heavy structure.\
Implement deterministic temporal variation using:\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f2 \cf2 \strokec2 effectiveSeed = hash(baseSeed, frameTimeOrFrameIndex)
\f1 \cf2 \strokec2 \
Requirements:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\ls6\ilvl0\cf2 \strokec2 {\listtext	\'95	}New streak positions and lengths across frames.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Per-frame brightness variation.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Stable overall vertical density gradient.\
{\listtext	\'95	}No obvious repeating short-cycle pattern.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Reproducible rendering for the same frame, seed, and settings.\
{\listtext	\'95	}An Animate With Time control.\
{\listtext	\'95	}A frozen mode that produces a stable pattern.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \strokec2 Use the host\'92s render time and appropriate AE timing information. Do not depend on render-call order, global mutable random state, or non-deterministic thread execution.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf2 \strokec2 6. Parameters and Controls\cf2 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf2 \strokec2 Expose the following controls in the preset:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\ls7\ilvl0
\f0\b \cf2 \strokec2 {\listtext	1.	}Streak Density
\f1\b0 \cf2 \strokec2  \'97 controls the overall number and probability of streak segments.\
\ls7\ilvl0
\f0\b \cf2 \strokec2 {\listtext	2.	}Horizontal Length
\f1\b0 \cf2 \strokec2  \'97 controls the average segment length and its variation.\
\ls7\ilvl0
\f0\b \cf2 \strokec2 {\listtext	3.	}Bottom Density Gradient
\f1\b0 \cf2 \strokec2  \'97 controls how strongly streak density increases toward the bottom.\
\ls7\ilvl0
\f0\b \cf2 \strokec2 {\listtext	4.	}Streak Brightness
\f1\b0 \cf2 \strokec2  \'97 controls the brightness of generated segments.\
\ls7\ilvl0
\f0\b \cf2 \strokec2 {\listtext	5.	}Streak Contrast
\f1\b0 \cf2 \strokec2  \'97 controls separation between dim and bright streaks.\
\ls7\ilvl0
\f0\b \cf2 \strokec2 {\listtext	6.	}Animate With Time
\f1\b0 \cf2 \strokec2  \'97 enables or freezes temporal variation.\
\ls7\ilvl0
\f0\b \cf2 \strokec2 {\listtext	7.	}Random Seed
\f1\b0 \cf2 \strokec2  \'97 controls deterministic pattern variation.\
\ls7\ilvl0
\f0\b \cf2 \strokec2 {\listtext	8.	}Input Blend
\f1\b0 \cf2 \strokec2  \'97 controls compositing with the original input.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \strokec2 Keep the parameter ranges useful and intuitive. Avoid redundant controls.\
The initial preset should approximate the reference\'92s medium-to-high streak density, strong bottom weighting, monochrome output, and clearly visible lower-region streaks.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf2 \strokec2 7. Compositing Modes\cf2 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf2 \strokec2 Support the existing VHSart compositing architecture.\
Where available, provide:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\ls8\ilvl0\cf2 \strokec2 {\listtext	\'95	}Generated dark-field output.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Screen blending.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Add blending.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Adjustable blending with the original input.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \strokec2 The generated pattern must be usable over a dark background or other footage.\
Do not force the original image to remain visible when the user selects a fully generated output mode.\
Preserve the original input alpha unless the selected output mode explicitly requires another behavior.\
Correctly handle premultiplied alpha and avoid unwanted dark or bright edge artifacts.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf2 \strokec2 8. Native After Effects Requirements\cf2 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf2 \strokec2 Implement this as a native C++ After Effects effect using the project\'92s existing AE SDK integration.\
Preserve:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\ls9\ilvl0\cf2 \strokec2 {\listtext	\'95	}After Effects parameter registration and UI conventions.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Existing project build configuration.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Multi-Frame Rendering compatibility.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Thread safety.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Deterministic frame rendering.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Correct pixel-format handling.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Alpha and premultiplication behavior.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Existing plugin version and PiPL consistency.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \strokec2 Do not introduce unnecessary external dependencies or pre-rendered assets.\
The entire visual effect must be generated mathematically during rendering. Do not use images, videos, GIFs, or pre-rendered overlays as substitutes for the procedural effect.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf2 \strokec2 9. Visual Validation\cf2 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf2 \strokec2 Build and test the actual native plugin in After Effects.\
Compare the output against 
\f2 \cf2 \strokec2 video_1.mov
\f1 \cf2 \strokec2  at synchronized timestamps, including:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\ls10\ilvl0\cf2 \strokec2 {\listtext	\'95	}00:00.000\
{\listtext	\'95	}00:00.250\
{\listtext	\'95	}00:00.500\
{\listtext	\'95	}00:00.750\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \strokec2 Inspect at 100% and 200% magnification.\
Validate:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\ls11\ilvl0\cf2 \strokec2 {\listtext	1.	}The upper region remains relatively sparse.\
{\listtext	2.	}Density increases smoothly toward the bottom.\
{\listtext	3.	}The bottom region contains clearly visible, closely spaced horizontal segments.\
{\listtext	4.	}The streaks remain monochrome.\
{\listtext	5.	}The effect does not introduce circular noise, chromatic artifacts, or geometric distortion.\
{\listtext	6.	}Streak positions and lengths change between frames.\
{\listtext	7.	}The overall bottom-heavy distribution remains stable over time.\
{\listtext	8.	}Frozen mode produces a stable result.\
{\listtext	9.	}Existing VHSart presets continue to work correctly.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \strokec2 Do not claim visual matching without actually comparing rendered output against the supplied reference.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

